WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.590
What do a lipstick, a microwave, and car paint
have in common?

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.550
I bet the question caught you by surprise.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:10.670
Well, should you want to analyze the manufacturing
process of each of these products, you'll

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.450
find that in all three cases mica is used.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:19.650
Mica, from the Latin word "mico"-"I shine"-is
a very special group of minerals: in fact,

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:25.180
their easy and perfect flaking, even by simple
rubbing with fingers, splits them into very

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:31.509
thin but elastic and flexible foils and scales,
with a characteristic mother-of-pearl luster.

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:36.430
Their versatility of use is remarkable: in
addition to the possibility of being combined

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.340
with other layers of material, they can be
ground and used in the form of powders or

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.040
flakes and possess a natural low electrical
and thermal conductivity.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.230
Because of these properties, it's possible
to find their use in most cosmetics on the

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:56.239
market, such as eye shadows and foundations,
but also in making paints, oven windows, heating

00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:57.500
systems, and even toothpastes.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:03.980
Of course, just as with other minerals, mica
must be sorted, mined and processed before

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.049
it's placed on the market for sale.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:10.170
If you have never heard of them, perhaps I
can also explain why.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:15.250
According to the Observatory of Economic Complexity
at the Institute of Technology in Cambridge,

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:21.240
Massachusetts, in 2021 the market for micas
had a total commercial value of two hundred

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.930
and thirty seven million dollars.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:31.680
In purely economic terms, these minerals participate
in only 0,000011% of the global market.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.630
A trifle in practice, when put in relation
to their variety of uses.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:40.510
The country that exported the largest amount,
in monetary terms, was China, with a total

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.149
of sixty-one million dollars.

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:46.649
This was followed by The Netherlands, India,
Madagascar and France.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:52.530
In terms of imports, however, the main buyers
turn out to be Japan, China, Germany, the

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.480
United States and Belgium.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.170
Until a few years ago, the use of mica in
cosmetic products was a source of pride for

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:04.030
the major multinationals in the sector, because
these are elements that are already present

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:09.229
in nature and t herefore not synthesized in
laboratories, which allows them to add the

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.930
"natural" stamp to their makeup of choice.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.150
This was, as I said, until a few years ago.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:19.470
Today, I want to focus on two of the nations
I just mentioned-India and Madagascar.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:24.110
Similar to what happens in other so-called
underdeveloped or developing countries, the

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.670
logic of profit involves costs beyond those
in money.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:33.620
I am talking, in this case, about the exploitation
of labor, which, unfortunately, also and especially

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.200
concerns children.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.090
And to talk about it, I have referred to two
investigations centered on surveys, interviews

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:46.250
and field observations supported by statistics
regarding the volume of domestic mica trades.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.780
But we'll get to that slowly.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.050
Let's start with India.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:54.280
In 2016, a Thomson Reuters Foundation survey
conducted over three months in the Indian

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:59.860
states of Bihar, Jharkhand, Rajasthan and
Andhra Pradesh shed light on a widespread

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.140
reality of child labor in so-called ghost
mines.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:08.890
The main type mined in India is muscovite,
also known as white or common mica, which,

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:14.030
although it can be used as an insulating material,
is also used to give shine to make-up and

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.080
skincare products.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.780
According to information extracted from the
Zauba platform, which catalogs data regarding

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.630
Indian import/export, Bihar exported more
than one hundred thousand tons of mica in

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.769
2015.

00:03:26.769 --> 00:03:31.360
For the Indian Bureau of Mines, on the other
hand, the whole of India would have produced

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.860
about 20 thousand in the same year.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:39.360
According to Reuters, this huge discrepancy
is explained by the fact that 70 percent of

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:44.500
production depended on the illegal mining
of mica, conducted mostly in abandoned forests

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.810
and quarries.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:51.030
And here we come to the darker side of ghost
mining: the tender age of the victims involved.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:56.250
In fact, according to reports by the children's
rights advocacy association Bachpan Bachao

00:03:56.250 --> 00:04:02.680
Andolan, in June 2016 alone, 20 children died
in the mica mines, double the monthly average.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.950
In fact, widespread health risks related to
the lack of proper safety systems and continuous

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:13.780
exposure to dust include respiratory problems,
skin infections, and deep cuts.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.070
This happens because, in most cases, children
are forced to collect the mica with their

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:23.720
bare hands, and although these minerals aren't
harmful, the environment from which they are

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.230
extracted can be.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.820
Unlike adults, moreover, children can enter
deeper cavities and so, more easily prone

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.930
to collapse, where they get to spend up to
eight hours.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.870
And they do it for a miserable pay.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:41.500
We are talking about between 50 and 300 rupees,
or between 80 cents and 4 dollars a day.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.950
Since in 90 percent of cases, these deaths
go unreported to local authorities, the actual

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.810
deaths could be far higher than those reported.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.110
"I didn't know how dangerous the work in the
mines is.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:58.610
Had i known, I would never have let him go,"
farmer Vasdev Rai Pratap, father of a 16-year-old

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.240
boy who died in June 2016 in Jharkhand, told
Reuters.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:06.810
"They said it took almost a day to dig out
his body after the mine collapsed.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:11.509
They cremated him without telling me."Pratap
then reveals that he accepted a payment of

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:15.160
one hundred thousand Indian rupees, equal
to $1,500.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:22.139
He did this in exchange for his silence to
avoid ending illegal mining on protected forest

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:25.360
lands that bring income to some of India's
poorest areas.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:30.540
By protected forest land Reuters refers to
the Forest Conservation Act, passed by India's

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:35.759
parliament in 1980, a directive that resulted
in a drastic reduction in mining and, in the

00:05:35.759 --> 00:05:41.919
specific case of mica, led to a reduction
in the 730 licensed quarries operating in

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:47.449
1964, to a maximum of 148 still active in
1986.

00:05:47.449 --> 00:05:53.169
And in 2014, the Indian Bureau of Mines reported
only two mica mining licenses in the entire

00:05:53.169 --> 00:05:56.790
state of Bihar, which is far from the reality
of the situation.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:03.169
As early as 1993, Sanjay Kumar had documented
in his book Problems and Prospects of Mineral

00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:08.160
Industry in India the existence of widespread
illegal mines especially in the Bihar Mica

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:13.370
belt that, although abandoned and lacking
machinery, were still being exploited to sell

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.669
the mineral to those who demanded it.

00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:21.030
It's possible to assume that unlicensed quarries,
hidden in dense forests, proliferated to meet

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:26.250
the constant domestic and international demand
for mica.To understand the phenomenon of ghost

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.780
mining, we need to dig deeper.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:34.150
Reuters' investigation is intertwined with
an interesting March 2016 report titled "Beauty

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:35.150
and a Beast."

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:39.730
It was published by the network of international
organizations Terre des Hommes, which fights

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:45.449
against child exploitation and discrimination,
in collaboration with SOMO, an independent

00:06:45.449 --> 00:06:49.880
Dutch research center investigating multinational
corporations.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:56.169
According to the data collected, in the year
2015/2016, underage workers amounted to about

00:06:56.169 --> 00:07:01.500
20,000, scattered in more than 300 villages
in the state of Jharkhand alone.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:06.879
Page 21 of the document lays out the percentages
of the population residing in the states of

00:07:06.879 --> 00:07:12.129
Jharkhand and Bihar living below the poverty
line, their literacy level, and the level

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:16.889
of education of children and teenagers between
the ages of 6 and 14.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:21.479
It immediately jumps out that these are much
worse data than the Indian average.

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:24.190
Which might suggest a link to child labor.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:29.699
It's likely, in fact, that children find themselves
working to make up, albeit with little pocket

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:34.360
money, for the economic condition of their
families, to the detriment of their education.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:39.860
Terre des Hommes also refers to another problem
endemic to the Indian reality: castes.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:44.610
According to a 2011 census referring to the
sub-districts of the two federated states

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:50.169
of Bihar and Jharkhand, in the largest of
them, namely Rajauli, Gawan and Domchanch,

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:55.409
the percentages of "dalits," the so-called
untouchables, or individuals of the lowest

00:07:55.409 --> 00:08:01.479
social status belonging to groups placed outside
the pattern of the 4 traditional castes, are

00:08:01.479 --> 00:08:05.360
29, 16 and 14 percent of the total population,
respectively.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:11.379
If this reality is still so widespread, despite
the formal abolition of untouchability and

00:08:11.379 --> 00:08:16.370
the discrimination that comes with it, what
are the Indian government and the multinational

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:20.530
corporations that import products from India
doing to counter it?

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:26.190
In January 2017, some 20 companies in the
cosmetics and electronics industries set up

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:31.229
the Responsible Mica Initiative, aimed at
funding educational and social projects to

00:08:31.229 --> 00:08:35.390
remove not only children, but also families,
from working in the mines.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:40.789
To date, more than 80 multinational companies
join, including Chanel, l'Oréal, Merck and

00:08:40.789 --> 00:08:41.789
Shiseido.

00:08:41.789 --> 00:08:44.220
Criticism, however, hasn't been slow in coming.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:49.500
First, it's worth noting that Beauty and a
Beast clearly mentions, in chapters 7 and

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.920
8, the major companies involved in the mica
market.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:57.720
Although Terre des Hommes and SOMO don't link
them directly to child labor, they accuse

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:03.990
them of supporting its perpetuation by continuing
to buy minerals from India.It's not hard to

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:09.240
imagine that these same companies, in anticipation
of enormous image damage, have run for cover.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:14.240
For example, pigment company Kuncai, the largest
importer of mica from Jharkhand and Bihar

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:22.149
in the first half of 2015, with 6200 tons
worth 201 million Indian rupees, immediately

00:09:22.149 --> 00:09:25.890
stated it would help Terre des Hommes “save"
10,000 children.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:30.589
The Jharkhand government also followed su
it, promising to legalize the mines to also

00:09:30.589 --> 00:09:33.260
regularize work activities within them.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:38.070
Unfortunately, however, it seems that nowadays
the situation hasn't changed at all.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:43.000
The pandemic hasn't only worsened the conditions
of those living in contact with mines but

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.410
has created a vacuum in terms of information
on the issue.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:52.080
In 2021, the Thomson Reuters Foundation again
called out multinational cosmetics companies.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.890
The reason was that the funds allocated to
the Responsible Mica Initiative, about a million

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:01.600
dollars a year, wouldn’t be used to combat
child labor, since children would seem to

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:06.570
continue to report infections and be victims
of accidents of various kinds.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.870
Then there is another problem on the horizon.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.640
There has been criticism of the world of make-up.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:16.420
Yet, the electronics industry has no less
impact on the global micas market.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:21.430
To realize this, let’s now switch hemispheres,
and move to a country that is in worse shape

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.170
than the Indian Federated States: Madagascar.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:29.350
We are talking, according to World Bank data,
about a purely agricultural nation that has

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.610
a poverty rate of 80 percent.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:36.540
This percentage of the population, in fact,
lives on little more than two dollars a day.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.040
According to the World Food Program, food
insecurity in Madagascar, also worsened by

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.540
frequent environmental disasters, involves
about 9 million people out of 28 total.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:51.591
If we admit the existence of a correlation
between poverty and child labor, what I am

00:10:51.591 --> 00:10:53.800
about to say will not surprise you.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:11:00.060
In 2018, according to UNICEF, 47 percent of
Malagasy children between the ages of 5 and

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:02.709
17 were employed as labor force.

00:11:02.709 --> 00:11:06.990
This reality is even more daunting in the
south of the country, which has been plagued

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:12.279
for nearly four decades by the anti-state
violence of so-called dahalo bandits, the

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:13.820
"cattle raiders."

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:19.529
According to Amnesty International, some 4,000
people, including thieves, civilians, security

00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:25.660
forces, and soldiers, died between 2015 and
2019 as a result of the government's hard

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.220
response to the dahalo.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:31.279
The raids and repression continue to this
day to claim victims.

00:11:31.279 --> 00:11:36.389
It's precisely in this context that most of
the mica mining activities, in which children

00:11:36.389 --> 00:11:38.160
are involved, are concentrated.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:43.860
In this regard, in 2019, three years after
Beauty and a Beast, Terre des Hommes and SOMO

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.470
released a new report.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:51.590
It found the presence on Malagasy territory
of 201 deposits of phlogopite, a mica that

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:57.360
is used in the manufacture of electrical and
thermal insulators, 176 of which would be

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:01.300
located in the southern regions of Ihorombe,
Androy and Anosy.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:06.079
The data strongly clashes with that reported
by the Bureau du Cadastre Minier de Madagascar,

00:12:06.079 --> 00:12:11.860
which, as of July 2019, recorded 50 valid
concessions for mica mining, or a quarter

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:13.790
of the mines actually exploited.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.060
How is this possible?

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:20.680
On page 23, the paper lays out what the supply
chain for mica is in Madagascar.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:25.959
About 20 thousand miners are involved in extracting
the required minerals, which are then acquired

00:12:25.959 --> 00:12:31.490
by 400 buyers, including independents and
employees of multinational companies operating

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:32.490
in the territory.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:37.000
Then it's the turn of the transporters, who
take the micas to five companies that are

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.760
responsible for sorting and dividing them.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:45.560
One of these is Tri-H, whose complex is located
in Tolagnaro, the capital of the Anosy region.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:50.990
It takes six hours of driving on narrow, unpaved
roads to reach the plant by truck.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:56.149
Finally, goods are piled up at Port d'Ehola,
built in 2009 by the Malagasy government and

00:12:56.149 --> 00:13:00.530
used as a docking port for cruise ships, cargo
ships, and reefers.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:05.430
Compared to mica mined in India, in Madagascar's
case this mineral goes to meet the needs of

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.440
different sectors and apparently has only
one interlocutor.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:15.450
In 2017, about 90 percent of the mica mined
in Madagascar was exported by sea to China,

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:20.870
where it was used as a component to produce
wires, cables and household appliances, as

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:23.250
well as finding use in the automotive industry.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:29.070
As Terre des Hommes shows on page 52 of its
report, the four main multinational corporations

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:35.089
importing Madagascar's mica are Chinese, and
engaged in the construction, hi-tech and electronics

00:13:35.089 --> 00:13:40.810
sectors, and would buy the mineral for a very
small sum: around 4 cents per kilo.

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:45.760
Now we come to the sorest note, the trait
that unites India and Madagascar in this circuit

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.950
centered on labor exploitation.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:54.019
Of the 20,000 Malagasy miners, at least 10,000
are between the ages of 5 and 17.

00:13:54.019 --> 00:13:59.580
Terre des Hommes has reported cases of very
young miners who are only fed at night because

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:04.660
they are constantly busy during the day, suffering
frequent back and headaches from too many

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:09.990
hours spent in uncomfortable positions and
oxygen deprivation inside the tunnels.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:15.570
In 2019, NBC conducted an investigation on
Malagasy soil, following in the footsteps

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:19.250
of Terre des Hommes, and quietly, without
announcing its arrival.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:25.130
Arriving in Amboasary South, 70km west of
Tolagnaro, reporters took photos of women

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:28.899
and children intent on sorting nearby mined
micas.

00:14:28.899 --> 00:14:33.560
The mothers interviewed confessed to earning
the equivalent of 3 dollars a week, working

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.220
for 13 hours a day.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:41.110
At the time, NBC asked for an interview with
Tri-H, whose manager, Haja Ranahary, said

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:46.840
he was aware of child labor in the mica mines,
adding, however, that "it's not our problem.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:51.209
It's not our fault, but the parents of the
children [...]. If it wasn't for the mica,

00:14:51.209 --> 00:14:55.240
all these people would be bandits and, right
now, they would be stealing cars."

00:14:55.240 --> 00:15:00.310
Data exposed by Terre des Hommes, however,
say that in the southern regions of Madagascar

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:06.570
only 12 percent of children finish secondary
school, and just 25 percent of the population

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.370
has access to clean water.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:12.899
Maybe, just maybe, it's the state that is
lacking, and it's the companies that are profiting

00:15:12.899 --> 00:15:13.899
from it.

00:15:13.899 --> 00:15:19.180
The multinationals surveyed, including Japan's
Panasonic, America's Electrolock and China's

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:24.820
CRRC said they were unaware of the reality
of child labor and would investigate their

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.339
own supply chains.

00:15:26.339 --> 00:15:31.320
The fact remains that widespread monitoring
is very difficult, in part because the confluence

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:36.670
of some of the mica extracted by Malagasy
children within the flow of mica from India

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:41.279
makes it virtually impossible to identify
the products into which it goes.

00:15:41.279 --> 00:15:46.690
And when we consider that many other companies
including Ford, Fiat, Isovolta, and Boeing

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:51.250
rely on mica sheets to make their cars and
airplanes, the plot thickens.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:55.550
Obviously, I don't have a solution to the
problem, nor am I here to tell you to stop

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.090
buying an eyeshadow or a car.

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:03.660
Unfortunately, although critical for its insulating
properties and resistance to high voltage,

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:08.069
mica is still a niche market, on which not
much of a spotlight is shining.

00:16:08.069 --> 00:16:10.930
In short, it's hard to see what goes where.

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:15.639
As I anticipated, several companies, such
as L'Oréal, haven’t given up on mica in

00:16:15.639 --> 00:16:20.690
favor of synthetics, continuing to purchase
it only "through a transparent and traceable

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:25.529
supply chain," in order to promote economic
development and improve the living conditions

00:16:25.529 --> 00:16:26.949
of Indian workers.

00:16:26.949 --> 00:16:32.139
Britain's Lush, on the other hand, had already
shown its intention in 2014 to remove all

00:16:32.139 --> 00:16:37.230
traces of so-called natural mica from its
products because of its connection to child

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:41.550
labor and, as of 2018, has switched to making
synthetic mica.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.519
Well, I am done here for today.

00:16:43.519 --> 00:16:48.430
The intention was to draw attention to a problem
that exists and is very little talked about.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:52.459
So I sincerely hope, despite the amount of
data, that I have managed to offer you a fairly

00:16:52.459 --> 00:16:54.800
clear and comprehensive analysis.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.279
Thanks for your attention and we’ll see
you in the next video.

00:16:58.279 --> 00:16:58.680
Ciao!

